  "Id": 1704,
  "Title": "English Course for AKU Drivers",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "AKU Drivers are improving their English with ELE_net",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<p></p><strong><p>A group of AKU drivers are currently doing an English course. The course is being  run through ELE_net's consultancy services offered to AKU departments. The content of the course is based on a series of common encounters drivers are likely to have with passengers in a typical working day. </p><br/><p>The course prioritises the development of learners' confidence when using English in these common work-related contexts. This is done through intensive listening and speaking practice leading to role plays acting out the situations drivers are likely to face. </p><br/><p>The drivers have been enthusiastic about the course. They are very motivated to improve their English for work and personal reasons: </p><br/><p>\" We need such opportunities to be able to communicate better with foreign clients\"- Saleh </p><br/><p>\" I can now talk to my children in English and they say very good to me\"- Raees</p></strong>",
